Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs(agents): issues work on their own branch from latest
 main, finish as a pushed PR, and a cut goes PR review -> merge -> tag

- Issue Law: sync main, branch issue/N-<slug>, push + PR with Fixes #N
  instead of committing to main; `in-review` label once the PR is open
  (the pick query skips it); changelog rows written at the cut from each
  PR's Changelog: line.
- Commits and Releases: a cut reviews and merges the issue PRs (merge
  commits), runs the release gate on release/vX.Y.Z, opens a release PR,
  then tags main's merge commit.
- scripts/release.ps1 gains -NoTag for the release branch.
- RECOMMENDED.md records the decisions filling in the mechanics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
